  "result": "All 1905 tests pass.\n\nI made the two truly-internal-only utilities private by prefixing with an underscore, since they aren't referenced by any tests or docs:\n\n- `click.utils.safecall` \u2192 `click.utils._safecall` (used only internally in `types.py`)\n- `click.utils.PacifyFlushWrapper` \u2192 `click.utils._PacifyFlushWrapper` (used only internally in `core.py`)\n\nI left `LazyFile`, `KeepOpenFile`, and `make_default_short_help` (the closest match to \"make_short_help\") as public names, since `LazyFile` is documented in `docs/handling-files.md` and all three are directly exercised by tests via `click.utils.LazyFile`, `click.utils.KeepOpenFile`, and `click.utils.make_default_short_help` \u2014 renaming them would require touching tests/docs, which I was told not to modify.\n\nFull test suite (1905 passed, 25 skipped, 1 xfailed) confirms nothing broke.",
